On Tue, Jun 23, 2009 at 11:42 AM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> So here's an off-the-wall question.  Would the three following sentences
> mean the same thing (emphasis and all)?
>
> klama
> zo'e klama zo'e zo'e zo'e zo'e
> lo klama cu klama lo se klama lo te klama lo ve klama lo xe klama


I'd say they all mean the same thing. The first two are technically
equivalent, although I imagine most hearers would seek an agenda behind all
those {zo'e}. Also, of course, the first could be interpreted as an
observative, while the others could not. The third, I think, is
tautological.

mu'o mi'e komfo,amonan

